Thought: To identify the organic compound and provide its SMILES code, I should start by gathering spectral data. The most informative initial step would be to obtain the mass spectrometry spectra to determine the molecular weight and possible molecular formula of the compound.
Action: mass_spectrometry_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: The mass spectrometry data indicates a molecular ion peak at m/z 193.11, which suggests the molecular weight of the compound is approximately 193.11 g/mol. To narrow down the possible molecular formula, I should now obtain the 13C NMR spectra to gather information about the carbon framework of the compound.
Action: carbon_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: Since the 13C NMR prediction failed, I should try obtaining the 1H NMR spectra to gather information about the hydrogen environment, which can also provide insights into the structure of the compound.
Action: proton_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: With both the 13C and 1H NMR predictions failing, I should attempt to use the IR spectra to identify functional groups present in the compound, which can help in deducing the structure.
Action: ir_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: The IR spectra show peaks that suggest the presence of O-H (3423, 3390 cm-1), C-H (3105-2915 cm-1), and a carbonyl group (1739 cm-1). This indicates the compound might be an alcohol or phenol with a carbonyl group, possibly an ester or carboxylic acid. To further narrow down the structure, I should determine the possible molecular formula using the mass spectrometry data and then explore possible isomers.
Action: retrieve_dbe_formula
